# Copy this file to .env for local development (SQLite).
DATABASE_URL="file:./dev.db"

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Production (Vercel) — RESERVED VARIABLE NAMES, PLACEHOLDER VALUES ONLY
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Do NOT put real credentials in this file — it's committed to the repo.
# Set the real value in the Vercel dashboard instead:
#   Project -> Settings -> Environment Variables -> DATABASE_URL
#   (check "Production", and "Preview" too if preview deploys need a DB)
#
# The placeholder below shows the exact shape Prisma expects for Postgres.
# Replace every part in <angle brackets> with the real value from your
# provider (Vercel Postgres, Neon, Supabase, etc.) — never commit the result.
#
#   DATABASE_URL="postgresql://<user>:<password>@<host>:5432/<database>?sslmode=require"
#
# Common provider dashboards call this the "Prisma" or "Connection string
# (URL)" field. If your provider gives you a pooled AND a direct URL, use
# the pooled one for DATABASE_URL (see DATABASE.md for details).
